    "rawOriginal": "---\nworkbench:\n  schema: 1\n  id: \"c442643b-d4de-4d31-a053-b01b69251a7d\"\n  title: \"Scene 06 — Arrival Hall\"\n  type: scene\n  purpose: session\n  status: draft\n---\n# Scene 06 — Arrival Hall\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe Arrival Hall gives the players their first glimpse of Whispering Reef Sanctuary as an ancient civilization, rather than a dungeon entrance. Pause and let them absorb its scale before encouraging exploration.\n\n**Desired emotional transition**\n\n**Committed → Wonder**\n\n---\n\n## Original Purpose\n\nEvery visitor passed through this hall: travelling Sea Guardians crossing the reef, merfolk emissaries, pilgrims, scholars and messengers. Here they were welcomed before being guided deeper into the sanctuary. The chamber served hospitality, never defence.\n\n---\n\n## Scene Setup\n\nAs the party emerges from the flooded passage, the crashing waves fall silent. Only dripping water remains. Allow a few seconds of silence before reading the description.\n\n---\n\n## Read Aloud\n\nYou pull yourselves from the cold seawater onto smooth stone.\n\nThe air is cool but surprisingly fresh.\n\nBefore you stretches a vast natural cavern unlike anything you have ever seen.\n\nTowering columns of living coral rise from crystal-clear pools, merging seamlessly into the surrounding reef.\n\nSunlight pours through narrow shafts high above, scattering shimmering patterns across the floor like moving stars beneath the sea.\n\nGentle streams wind through carefully carved channels before disappearing into the depths of the sanctuary.\n\nNothing here feels conquered.\n\nNothing feels forced.\n\nIt is impossible to tell where nature ends...\n\nand where careful hands once began.\n\nFor a long moment...\n\nthe sanctuary says nothing.\n\nIt simply waits.\n\n---\n\n## What the Players Notice\n\nWithout making any checks:\n\n- The chamber is immense.\n- Living coral has been cultivated rather than left to grow wild.\n- Every water channel appears intentional.\n- There are no doors—only graceful stone archways.\n- The architecture feels organic, almost grown instead of built.\n- The sanctuary is remarkably intact despite its age.\n\n---\n\n## Exploration / Investigation\n\n### The Welcome Basin\n\nSeveral tiny streams feed a shallow circular basin at the hall's centre. Its perfectly clear water feels cool and exceptionally clean. Travellers once washed away salt here before entering the sanctuary.\n\n### Stone Relief\n\nA wall relief depicts humans, sea elves, merfolk, tritons and a goliath working together. No figure stands above another; none bears a crown or weapon. Even without words, the message is clear: the Order was united by purpose, not blood.\n\n### Water Channels\n\nCharacters following the channels notice they all flow deeper into the sanctuary.\n\nWhatever lies ahead is literally the heart of this place.\n\n---\n\n## Atmosphere\n\n> **TODO — Campaign Horror System**\n\nChoose one subtle event.\n\nSuggestions:\n\n- A ray of sunlight shifts although no clouds pass overhead.\n- A distant splash echoes through the sanctuary.\n- One character briefly thinks they hear quiet chanting, but it is only flowing water.\n- Tiny fish dart through a channel before disappearing into darkness.\n\n---\n\n## Player Questions\n\n### \"Has this place really been abandoned for centuries?\"\n\nEverything suggests yes.\n\nNature has reclaimed much of the sanctuary.\n\nYet the craftsmanship remains unmistakable.\n\n### \"Can we identify the builders?\"\n\nNot yet.\n\nTheir identity remains a mystery.\n\nThe players only know that many peoples contributed.\n\n---\n\n## Running the Scene\n\nLet the players look before investigating. If they begin discussing who built this place, the scene has succeeded. Resist explaining it: preserve their wonder rather than supplying answers.\n\n---\n\n## Thomas\n\nThomas slowly turns in place.\n\nHis voice is barely above a whisper.\n\n\"This...\n\n...this is beautiful.\"\n\nHe seems relieved.\n\nThe uneasy pull that brought him here has vanished.\n\nFor the first time since leaving Blacktide Haven, he is no longer looking toward the sea.\n\nHe is looking at the sanctuary.\n\n---\n\n## Transition\n\nSeveral natural passages lead deeper into the complex. The broadest follows the water toward the Hall of Tides.\n\nContinue with **[Scene 07 — Hall of Tides](04%20-%20hall_of_tides.md)**.\n\n---\n\n## DM Notes\n\nThis hall establishes the Sea Guardians' visual identity. Carry these ideas into the rest of the sanctuary:\n\n- Harmony with nature.\n- Quiet purpose.\n- A civilization that served rather than ruled.\n\nInspire awe rather than fear here; the horror comes later.\n\n---\n\n## Future Callbacks\n\n- The relief establishes that the Sea Guardians were an Order composed of many peoples.\n- The flowing water foreshadows the importance of the Waterworks and Ritual Pool.\n- The architecture becomes the visual language of every future Sea Guardian sanctuary.\n",
