    "sourceHash": "38c79ad779199dec1b62fec857b4ccddd4f0b2d6a2b0902e603a02d214ab6b82",
    "rawOriginal": "---\nworkbench:\n  schema: 1\n  id: \"833a7f1f-78ec-4bc6-b75a-950baadf467e\"\n  title: \"Agelus Trail — Playable Investigation Scenes\"\n  type: adventure\n  purpose: session\n  status: draft\n---\n# Agelus Trail — Playable Investigation Scenes\n\n> **Campaign Book — DM Only**\n> **Scope:** Tordeck's belongings → Monastery → Tordeck's island → Greenbank Farm → southern expedition\n> **Supporting handouts:** Notebook 1, Seed Chest table, Papers from Agelus's Worktable, Agelus Network Map\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe Company follows **Agelus the person**, then **the things he noticed**, and at Greenbank discovers **the idea he developed**. They find him by learning how he thought, not by following conveniently abandoned journals.\n\n**Notebook + Seed Chest → Monastery testimony → Tordeck remembers his island → Island ecology → Greenbank Farm → Distribution Map → J**\n\nEssential evidence must never depend on one successful skill check.\n\n## Scenes\n\nChoose scenes explicitly when preparing a session. Linked scenes and handouts are separate material.\n\n1. [Tordeck's Chest](scenes/01_tordecks_chest.md)\n2. [The Monastery Garden](scenes/02_monastery_garden.md)\n3. [Tordeck Remembers](scenes/03_tordeck_remembers.md)\n4. [The Island That Remembers](scenes/04_island_that_remembers.md)\n5. [Greenbank Farm](scenes/05_greenbank_farm.md)\n6. [Reading Agelus's Map](scenes/06_reading_agelus_map.md)\n7. [Preparing for J](scenes/07_preparing_for_j.md)\n\n## Investigation Safety Net\n\n### Tordeck → Monastery\n\nPrimary: **BH-N11**.\n\nBackup: Tordeck remembers Agelus left intending to inspect a reported northern Brineheart population.\n\n### Monastery → Tordeck's Island\n\nPrimary: monk remembers the Stormpea surprise and Agelus's connection to Tordeck.\n\nBackup: **SP-T02** becomes meaningful once Stormpea is discussed.\n\n### Island → Greenbank\n\nPrimary: feral Sailor's Kale matches **SK-G12**.\n\nAlternative: trace seed suppliers, agricultural contacts, or Greenbank references in Notebook 1.\n\nBackup: Tordeck or Corin can identify Greenbank as the named farm after the players surface SK-G12.\n\n### Greenbank → J\n\nPrimary: map + final expedition note + farmer testimony.\n\nThis information is intentionally preserved and requires no check.\n\n---\n\n## NPC Guidance Rule\n\nTordeck and Corin help players **recover established information**.\n\nThey may:\n\n- remind them that a name appeared in Notebook 1;\n- identify a known Church institution or region;\n- remember a conversation once new context makes it relevant;\n- ask a question that puts two known facts together.\n\nThey should not:\n\n- solve botanical conclusions for the Company;\n- know Agelus's mature theory;\n- identify Sea Guardian centers from the map;\n- reveal what J or K contains.\n\n**NPCs restore context. Players make discoveries.**\n\n---\n\n## Supporting Material\n\n- [Notebook 1](agelus_notebook_1.md)\n- [Seed chest](seed_chest_content.md)\n\nPapers from Agelus's Worktable is currently an empty source file. The mature map is described in design material; a finished player handout is not supplied here.\n",
