    "rawOriginal": "---\nworkbench:\n  schema: 1\n  id: \"726a03fe-d633-4b2c-9322-cc931f7fd4b0\"\n  title: \"Scene 1 — Tordeck's Chest\"\n  type: scene\n  purpose: session\n  status: draft\n---\n# Scene 1 — Tordeck's Chest\n\n## Purpose\n\nBegin the father investigation with something personal and useful.\n\nTordeck gives the Company:\n\n- Agelus's Notebook 1;\n- his seed chest;\n- the first evidence that Agelus's interest in difficult crops had become an investigation.\n\nNotebook 1 ends before Agelus travels to the monastery. It contains questions, not answers.\n\n## Running the Scene\n\nGive the players Notebook 1 and the seed chest together.\n\nMatch the notebook identifiers to the chest labels. These are Agelus's working samples, not treasure assembled for the Company.\n\nThe important entries are:\n\n- **BH-F03** — Broken Atoll Brineheart;\n- **BH-N11** — reported northern monastery Brineheart;\n- **SP-F05** — Broken Atoll Stormpea associated with disturbed/enriched ground;\n- **SP-T02** — Tordeck's description of peas from his old island;\n- **SK-G12** — Greenbank Farm Sailor's Kale.\n\nDo not make Tordeck remember the significance of his island immediately. At this point, the clearest unfinished intention in Agelus's notebook is the monastery.\n\n## Likely Conclusion\n\nThe lead is Agelus's intention to see the monastery's Brineheart himself.\n\n## Safety Net\n\nIf the players miss it, Tordeck can ask what Agelus still intended to investigate when he left the notebook.\n\nCorin can identify the monastery as a real Church-connected location after the players point out BH-N11.\n\nNPCs restore context. They do not solve the clue.\n\n## Related Material\n\n- [Adventure overview](../agelus_trail_playable_scenes.md)\n- [Notebook 1](../agelus_notebook_1.md)\n- [Seed chest](../seed_chest_content.md)\n- [Next scene](02_monastery_garden.md)\n",
