    "rawOriginal": "---\nworkbench:\n  schema: 1\n  id: \"2b394065-1d4a-4eac-bd9c-22424cb9fbb1\"\n  title: \"Scene 2 — The Monastery Garden\"\n  type: scene\n  purpose: session\n  status: draft\n---\n# Scene 2 — The Monastery Garden\n\n## Purpose\n\nConfirm that Agelus reached the monastery seeking **Brineheart**, then unexpectedly found **Stormpea**.\n\nThe scene answers:\n\n> Did Agelus come here, and what interested him?\n\nIt raises:\n\n> Why did Stormpea make him think of Tordeck?\n\n## Original Purpose\n\nThe garden feeds and supports the monastery. Generations of monks have propagated an old Brineheart lineage for its usefulness, without knowing its origin. Its plants are not a puzzle.\n\nThe wider landscape preserves traces of older cultivation associated with a minor Sea Guardian station, but the monastery is not a major sanctuary.\n\n## Scene Setup\n\nFollowing BH-N11, the Company finds the Brineheart they expected: hardy stock growing against old sheltered stone despite the northern climate.\n\nIf the Company carries the seed chest, BH-F03 provides an immediate comparison: the monastery stock resembles the old Broken Atoll stock more closely than Agelus's southern reference.\n\n## The Monk Who Remembers Agelus\n\nUse an older monk who remembers Agelus because of how intensely interested he became in things the monks considered ordinary.\n\nHe remembers that Agelus:\n\n- measured leaves;\n- examined tubers;\n- asked how long the monastery had propagated them;\n- compared the plants with notes and samples from elsewhere;\n- received the inevitable answer that the monks had grown them for as long as anyone remembered.\n\nThen Agelus noticed something else.\n\n## The Surprise — Stormpea\n\nStormpea grows beyond the active vegetable beds.\n\nIt survives around:\n\n- old terraces;\n- former worked ground;\n- soil beside walls no longer used as gardens.\n\nThe monks consider it an ordinary hardy pea. Agelus instead spent part of a day exploring these old areas, setting aside the Brineheart he had travelled north to study.\n\n## Suggested Recollection\n\n> \"The root brought him here. The peas kept him.\"\n>\n> \"He asked where we planted them. I told him we didn't, not those ones. They had been there longer than I had.\"\n>\n> \"After that he wanted to know where the old gardens had been. Not our gardens. The ones before them.\"\n>\n> \"He spoke of Tordeck after that. Said Tordeck had once told him of peas that remained even after the farms did not.\"\n\nThe monk does not know what Agelus concluded.\n\n## Optional Sea Guardian Trace\n\nA small Sea Guardian symbol may survive in reused old stonework.\n\nIt is a clue, not a revelation.\n\nIf recognized, the Company now has two facts sitting beside each other:\n\n- unusual old cultivation;\n- a trace of Sea Guardian presence.\n\nDo not explain the relationship.\n\n## Transition\n\nThe Company has reason to return to Tordeck and ask what Agelus knew about the peas on his island.\n\n## Related Material\n\n- [Adventure overview](../agelus_trail_playable_scenes.md)\n- [Previous scene](01_tordecks_chest.md)\n- [Next scene](03_tordeck_remembers.md)\n",
