    "rawOriginal": "---\nworkbench:\n  schema: 1\n  id: \"d0fa1f6b-4d31-4599-8967-1730a15d9e43\"\n  title: \"Scene 4 — The Island That Remembers\"\n  type: scene\n  purpose: session\n  status: draft\n---\n# Scene 4 — The Island That Remembers\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe Company makes the same conceptual leap Agelus made:\n\n> Plants can preserve vanished human activity.\n\nThere is no Notebook 2, map, or letter saying where Agelus went. The evidence is alive.\n\n## Arrival\n\nThe tsunami happened long enough ago for the island to turn green again. Show old destruction overgrown by nature, not fresh devastation.\n\n## Read Aloud\n\n> The island is greener than Tordeck's stories prepared you for.\n>\n> Trees lean above broken stone. Grass covers terraces that end abruptly at washed-out ground. Here and there a wall survives without the house it once belonged to.\n>\n> Nothing waits for you.\n>\n> No smoke. No footprints. No abandoned pack bearing Agelus's name.\n>\n> Only an island that has had years to grow over what happened here.\n\n## The Apparent Dead End\n\nThe Company can find:\n\n- foundations;\n- collapsed terraces;\n- old animal enclosures;\n- shell and ash in former household soils;\n- channels altered by the tsunami;\n- vegetation obscuring the settlement's old layout.\n\nThere may be subtle evidence that somebody investigated the ground years ago — moved stones, exposed soil, an old overgrown path — but nothing that points onward.\n\n## The Tool They Already Have\n\nNotebook 1 contains:\n\n**SP-T02** — Tordeck's peas.\n\n**SP-F05** — Agelus's observation that Stormpea thrives around disturbed and enriched soil.\n\nLet the players search for Stormpea.\n\n## Stormpea Distribution\n\nIt does not grow evenly.\n\nStrong old patches cluster around:\n\n- elevated former gardens;\n- terrace edges;\n- old animal pens;\n- soil enriched by shell, ash, bone, and household waste;\n- places where cultivated ground escaped the worst saltwater inundation.\n\nThe plant reveals the vanished settlement.\n\n## Running the Discovery\n\nDo not reduce the discovery to one Nature check. Reveal the pattern in stages:\n\n1. Stormpea grows beside an obvious terrace.\n2. Another patch reveals an old enclosure.\n3. A patch grows where no visible building survives; examining its soil reveals old human enrichment.\n\nLet the Company reach the conclusion:\n\n**the plants remember where people cultivated the land.**\n\nThis is what Agelus came to test.\n\n## If They Stall\n\nEscalate evidence rather than giving the answer.\n\n1. Someone recognizes Stormpea from the notebook.\n2. A patch grows beside an obvious terrace.\n3. Tordeck's description can be recalled.\n4. Only then may an NPC suggest comparing the pea patches with the old settlement.\n\n## The Second Plant — SK-G12\n\nDuring the search, the Company finds feral Sailor's Kale with:\n\n- broad leaves;\n- the distinctive pale line along the central leaf rib.\n\nNotebook 1 describes the same traits under:\n\n**SK-G12 — Greenbank Farm stock**\n\nThe chest contains SK-G12 and the original Greenbank wrapping.\n\nOnce the players inspect the kale, make this connection easy to recover. The difficult discovery was learning how to read the island.\n\n## What the Kale Means\n\nSailor's Kale spreads too easily to prove that Greenbank supplied this island population. It does establish Greenbank as a real agricultural contact Agelus knew, used, and wanted to visit: enough for the Company to investigate his later movements.\n\n## Alternate Routes to Greenbank\n\nIf the players instead trace:\n\n- Agelus's seed suppliers;\n- agricultural contacts;\n- provenance labels;\n- Greenbank's name in Notebook 1;\n\nthose methods should also reach the farm.\n\nThe kale is the strongest clue, not a mandatory key.\n\n## Transition\n\nThe island explains why Agelus came, but not where he went. The Company now has a real-world contact to investigate: **Greenbank Farm.**\n\n## Related Material\n\n- [Adventure overview](../agelus_trail_playable_scenes.md)\n- [Previous scene](03_tordeck_remembers.md)\n- [Next scene](05_greenbank_farm.md)\n",
