    "rawOriginal": "---\nworkbench:\n  schema: 1\n  id: \"508601dc-396e-4af8-9e44-8696aa718b0f\"\n  title: \"Scene 6 — Reading Agelus's Map\"\n  type: scene\n  purpose: session\n  status: draft\n---\n# Scene 6 — Reading Agelus's Map\n\n## Purpose\n\nGive the Company room to make the campaign-level deduction, at Greenbank or later aboard the Sea Witch.\n\n## The Key Comparison\n\nAgelus independently marks the Broken Atoll as one of his strongest historical centers. The Company has explored Whispering Reef and knows there is a Sea Guardian sanctuary there; Agelus did not.\n\nThe available deduction is:\n\n> Agelus may have reconstructed part of the Sea Guardian network without knowing what the Sea Guardians were.\n\nThis should belong to the players.\n\n## Corin's Role\n\nIf the table stalls, Corin can put known facts beside each other:\n\n> \"The Broken Atoll is one of his circles. What did you find there that Agelus never did?\"\n\nHe should not identify the network himself.\n\n## What Changes\n\nJ is now simultaneously:\n\n- Agelus's final known destination;\n- a test of his botanical model;\n- a possible second Sea Guardian center.\n\nThat makes the next expedition matter on personal, scientific, and historical levels.\n\n## Related Material\n\n- [Adventure overview](../agelus_trail_playable_scenes.md)\n- [Previous scene](05_greenbank_farm.md)\n- [Next scene](07_preparing_for_j.md)\n",
